codex
The first symbolic run exposed a useful proof-engineering issue: the comprehension allocates a fresh list on every accepted element, which makes the loop invariant depend on an unbounded heap-freshness argument. I’m switching to the equivalent in-place `append` loop already supported by the reference semantics. It has the same Python contract but admits a clean induction invariant over the input sequence and one stable accumulator object.
apply patch
